  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper benchmarks classical ML and hybrid quantum ML for fraud detection on the IBM AML dataset. Classical models outperform quantum ones: Random Forest achieves 97.34% accuracy and F-measure 0.8695, while the best quantum model (QSVC with 4 qubits) reaches 92.9% accuracy and F-measure 0.5372 with recall 0.412. Variational models (VQC and HQNN) perform poorly, with F-measure as low as 0.0–0.21.",
